{%- comment -%}
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  CWC CART LINE ITEM
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  The cart drawer's line item. This is a drawer-only presentation of a cart line — `snippets/line-item.liquid` stays as
  it is for the order page and the cart page, which have a different layout and different rules.

  EVERY figure here comes from the `line_item` object. Nothing is computed, stored or cached.

  FUNCTIONAL HOOKS. Three things in here are read by `assets/theme.js` and must not be renamed or re-nested:

    <line-item>           `changeLineItemQuantity` calls `.closest('line-item')` to fire `line-item:will-change` and
                          `line-item:change` on the right row.
    <line-item-quantity>  is the delegate root. It listens for `change` on `[data-line-key]` and for `click` on
                          `[href*="/cart/change"]`. BOTH the quantity stepper and the remove link are such hrefs, so
                          both have to stay INSIDE this element or they fall back to a full page navigation.
    quantity-selector     renders the `data-line-key` input and the two cart/change anchors.

  THREE MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE SHAPES. Membership and kit are separate product concepts that do not overlap, so each
  owns the whole card rather than decorating the standard one:

    membership  `CWC_cart_membership_line` — its own card. The line is handed over entirely.
                CURRENTLY OFF via `membership_line_enabled` — these lines render as standard for now.
    kit         inline below — collapses several products into one row and adds a component disclosure.
    standard    everything else.

  ********************************************
  Supported variables
  ********************************************

  * line_item: the cart line to render (required)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign kit_components = line_item.product.metafields.custom.kit_components.value
  assign kit_component_count = 0

  comment
    A component with no product reference cannot be named or counted, so it is
    skipped rather than printed as a blank row.
  endcomment
  for component in kit_components
    if component.product.value != blank
      assign kit_component_count = kit_component_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor

  assign is_kit = false
  if kit_component_count > 1
    assign is_kit = true
  endif

  comment
    A membership line is a subscription line whose product carries gift entries.
    The selling plan is what the add-to-cart request supplies; the gifts are read
    off the product here. Missing either one and the line is not a membership.

    TEMPORARILY DISABLED. `membership_line_enabled` is false, so these lines fall
    through to the standard product card and show as ordinary products for now.
    The detection below is deliberately left intact — flip the flag back to true
    to restore the gift display, nothing else needs changing.
  endcomment
  assign membership_line_enabled = false

  assign membership_gifts = line_item.product.metafields.custom.membership_gifts.value
  assign is_membership = false

  if membership_line_enabled and line_item.selling_plan_allocation and membership_gifts.size > 0
    assign is_membership = true
  endif

  comment
    THE STRUCK-THROUGH FIGURE is the highest honest "before" price for this line.

    Two independent things can lower what is actually paid, and either, both or
    neither may be in play:

      compare-at  the merchant's own was-price on the variant. Per unit, so it
                  is multiplied by the line quantity to sit beside a line total.
      discounts   a code or automatic discount, which is what moves
                  original_line_price down to final_line_price.

    Taking the greater of the two leaves one strikethrough that is never lower
    than the price printed beside it. Showing the smaller of them next to a
    deeper discount would understate the saving; showing both would ask the
    shopper to do the arithmetic.
  endcomment
  assign compare_at_line_price = 0

  if line_item.variant.compare_at_price > line_item.variant.price
    assign compare_at_line_price = line_item.variant.compare_at_price | times: line_item.quantity
  endif

  assign was_line_price = compare_at_line_price

  if line_item.original_line_price > was_line_price
    assign was_line_price = line_item.original_line_price
  endif
-%}

{%- capture line_item_body -%}
  <div class="cwc_cart__line">
    <div class="cwc_cart__line-media">
      {%- if line_item.image != blank -%}
        {{-
          line_item.image
          | image_url: width: line_item.image.width
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'lazy',
            sizes: '74px',
            widths: '74,148,222',
            class: 'cwc_cart__line-image',
            alt: line_item.title
        -}}
      {%- else -%}
        {{- 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'cwc_cart__line-image' -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="cwc_cart__line-body">
      <div class="cwc_cart__line-top">
        <div class="cwc_cart__line-ident">
          {%- if is_kit -%}
            <span class="cwc_cart__line-tag">Kit &middot; {{ kit_component_count }} products</span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if line_item.url != blank -%}
            <a href="{{ line_item.url }}" class="cwc_cart__line-name">
              {{- line_item.product.title | default: line_item.title -}}
            </a>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="cwc_cart__line-name">{{ line_item.product.title | default: line_item.title }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The strikethrough is the line's own original price. It appears only when
          a discount actually moved it, so an undiscounted line never prints a
          decorative "was" figure.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cwc_cart__line-prices">
          <span class="cwc_cart__line-price">
            {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
              {{- line_item.final_line_price | money_with_currency -}}
            {%- else -%}
              {{- line_item.final_line_price | money -}}
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>

          {%- if was_line_price > line_item.final_line_price -%}
            <span class="cwc_cart__line-was">
              <span class="sr-only">{{ 'product.price.regular_price' | t }}</span>

              {%- if settings.currency_code_enabled -%}
                {{- was_line_price | money_with_currency -}}
              {%- else -%}
                {{- was_line_price | money -}}
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- capture line_item_variant -%}
        {%- unless line_item.product.has_only_default_variant or line_item.gift_card -%}
          {{- line_item.variant.title -}}
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- if line_item_variant != blank -%}
        <span class="cwc_cart__line-variant">{{ line_item_variant | strip }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The selling plan name is the subscription cadence. Without a plan the line
        is a one-time purchase, and saying so is what tells the two apart at a glance.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if line_item.selling_plan_allocation -%}
        <span class="cwc_cart__line-plan">{{ line_item.selling_plan_allocation.selling_plan.name }}</span>
      {%- else -%}
        {% comment %} <span class="cwc_cart__line-plan cwc_cart__line-plan--once">One-time purchase</span> {% endcomment %}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- unless line_item.properties == blank -%}
        {%- capture line_item_properties -%}
          {%- for property in line_item.properties -%}
            {%- assign first_character_in_key = property.first | truncate: 1, '' -%}

            {%- if property.last == blank or first_character_in_key == '_' -%}
              {%- continue -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            <li class="cwc_cart__line-property">
              {%- if property.last contains '/uploads/' -%}
                <a href="{{ property.last }}">{{ property.last | split: '/' | last }}</a>
              {%- else -%}
                {{ property.first }}: {{ property.last }}
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}

        {%- if line_item_properties != blank -%}
          <ul class="cwc_cart__line-properties" role="list">{{ line_item_properties }}</ul>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endunless -%}

      {%- if line_item.line_level_discount_allocations != blank -%}
        <ul class="cwc_cart__line-discounts" role="list">
          {%- for discount_allocation in line_item.line_level_discount_allocations -%}
            <li class="cwc_cart__line-discount">
              {%- render 'icon' with 'discount', width: 11 -%}
              {{ discount_allocation.discount_application.title }} (-{{ discount_allocation.amount | money }})
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        HOOK: line-item-quantity is the delegate root for both controls below.
        Moving either one outside it silently turns an Ajax update into a page load.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <line-item-quantity class="cwc_cart__line-foot">
        {%- render 'quantity-selector', line_item: line_item, size: 'sm' -%}

        <a
          href="{{ line_item.url_to_remove }}"
          class="cwc_cart__line-remove"
          aria-label="{{ 'cart.order.remove' | t | escape }}"
        >
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M4 7h16M9 7V5a1 1 0 011-1h4a1 1 0 011 1v2M6 7l1 13h10l1-13"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </line-item-quantity>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  A kit collapses to a single row. Its components are read-only: the quantity
  stepper and the remove link above act on the kit line, which is the only line
  the cart actually holds — the components are a description of it, not lines of
  their own, so giving them their own controls would promise an edit the cart
  cannot make.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if is_membership -%}
  {%- render 'CWC_cart_membership_line__block', line_item: line_item -%}
{%- elsif is_kit -%}
  <line-item class="cwc_cart__item cwc_cart__item--kit">
    <cwc-cart-bundle class="cwc_cart__bundle">
      {{ line_item_body }}

      <button
        type="button"
        class="cwc_cart__bundle-toggle"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="cwc-cart-bundle-{{ line_item.key }}"
        data-show-label="Show {{ kit_component_count }} items"
        data-hide-label="Hide {{ kit_component_count }} items"
      >
        <span class="cwc_cart__bundle-toggle-label">Show {{ kit_component_count }} items</span>
        {%- render 'icon' with 'chevron-down', width: 9, class: 'cwc_cart__bundle-caret' -%}
      </button>

      <div class="cwc_cart__bundle-items" id="cwc-cart-bundle-{{ line_item.key }}" hidden>
        {%- for component in kit_components -%}
          {%- assign component_product = component.product.value -%}
          {%- if component_product == blank -%}
            {%- continue -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="cwc_cart__bundle-item">
            <div class="cwc_cart__bundle-item-media">
              {%- if component_product.featured_image != blank -%}
                {{-
                  component_product.featured_image
                  | image_url: width: 168
                  | image_tag:
                    loading: 'lazy',
                    sizes: '42px',
                    widths: '42,84,126',
                    class: 'cwc_cart__bundle-item-image',
                    alt: component_product.title
                -}}
              {%- else -%}
                {{- 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'cwc_cart__bundle-item-image' -}}
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            <div class="cwc_cart__bundle-item-body">
              <span class="cwc_cart__bundle-item-name">{{ component_product.title }}</span>

              {%- if component.role != blank -%}
                <span class="cwc_cart__bundle-item-sub">{{ component.role }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              One kit line holds one of each component, so the printed count is the
              kit's own quantity: two kits hold two of everything inside them.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="cwc_cart__bundle-item-qty">&times;{{ line_item.quantity }}</span>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </cwc-cart-bundle>
  </line-item>
{%- else -%}
  <line-item class="cwc_cart__item">
    {{ line_item_body }}
  </line-item>
{%- endif -%}
